<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Daphnia magna ocellus-pigment Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, detail scale) (Daphnia magna)",
        "Daphnia magna ocellus-pigment Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Daphnia magna morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Daphnia magna specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Daphnia magna" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of a 2.736 µm ocellus stripe. That length is the assigned tier.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim an independent second assessor scored this pass.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the in-sample dispersion correlation is a held-out test. Odd modes are not yet withheld.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nine Fourier modes are grown from the unstable eigenvector. Pearson r and RMSE compare those rates with σ(k) on the band σ > -0.15. A D_u sweep and an equal-diffusion ablation are included.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The SEM scale bar and an interior peak of the cuticle spectrum (20.17 µm) are measured on the vendored image.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The length unit is chosen so λ_c = 2.736 µm. Parameters a = 0.062, b = 1.180, D_u = 0.016, D_v = 0.640 are not the slot-149 placeholders.",
        "reported_in_source: Macagno (1981) showed that the Daphnia magna visual system is built by cellular interactions. Smith & Macagno (1990) resolved four spectral classes inside single ommatidia. Hebert & Emery (1990) showed that cuticular melanin is an inducible ultraviolet shield.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength 2π/k_c from a dispersion relation. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v.",
        "transfer_boundary: Nothing here transfers to a claim that the ×130 cuticle polygons are a 2.736 µm pigment stripe.",
        "transfer_boundary: The age delta along this chronoseries is zero. The comparison with a melanosome (~0.5 µm) and an ommatidium (tens of µm) is a scale comparison, not a fossil sequence." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Daphnia magna" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Daphnia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/daphnia_magna_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Daphnia magna; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, note scipy 1.18 and Pillow 13 installed for this run; no virtualenv; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength 2π/k_c from a dispersion relation. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | Macagno (1981) showed that the Daphnia magna visual system is built by cellular interactions. Smith & Macagno (1990) resolved four spectral classes inside single ommatidia. Hebert & Emery (1990) showed that cuticular melanin is an inducible ultraviolet shield.; reconstructed_in_script: The length unit is chosen so λ_c = 2.736 µm. Parameters a = 0.062, b = 1.180, D_u = 0.016, D_v = 0.640 are not the slot-149 placeholders. | Nine Fourier modes are grown from the unstable eigenvector. Pearson r and RMSE compare those rates with σ(k) on the band σ > -0.15. A D_u sweep and an equal-diffusion ablation are included. | The SEM scale bar and an interior peak of the cuticle spectrum (20.17 µm) are measured on the vendored image.; transfer_boundary: The age delta along this chronoseries is zero. The comparison with a melanosome (~0.5 µm) and an ommatidium (tens of µm) is a scale comparison, not a fossil sequence. | Nothing here transfers to a claim that the ×130 cuticle polygons are a 2.736 µm pigment stripe.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of a 2.736 µm ocellus stripe. That length is the assigned tier. | Does not claim the in-sample dispersion correlation is a held-out test. Odd modes are not yet withheld. | Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present. | Does not claim an independent second assessor scored this pass.]; phenomenon_size: 2.9 µm (2.904e-06 m, log10=-5.537 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.9 µm to 4.6 mm): 2.9 µm:daphnia-magna-bioelectric-polarity, 5.4 µm:daphnia-magna-vertex-packing, 103 µm:daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength, 190 µm:daphnia-magna-clock-wavefront, 616 µm:daphnia-magna-morphogen-condensation, 802 µm:daphnia-magna-flux-canalization, 845 µm:daphnia-magna-elastic-buckling, 1.1 mm:daphnia-magna-branching-tree" ;
